    {
      "page_title": "Errors Are Values",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Interface",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "type error interface {",
            "  Error() string // that is all of it",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`error` is a built-in interface, not a language construct",
            "Any type with `Error() string` satisfies it",
            "No registration, no inheritance, no base class",
            "`var err error = myErr{}` — non-pointer struct works too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Return, Don't Throw",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No exceptions for ordinary failure in Go",
            "Functions return `(T, error)` — error is the last result",
            "Handled at the call site, never unwound past you",
            "Control flow stays visible in the source you read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "v, err := f()",
            "if err != nil {",
            "  return err // one line, no unwinding",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Java / Python",
                "lines": [
                  "throw",
                  "stack unwinds",
                  "catch far away",
                  "control flow hidden"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Go",
                "lines": [
                  "return err",
                  "caller checks",
                  "handle or wrap",
                  "flow in source"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "nil Means Success",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Zero value of `error` is `nil`",
            "`nil` means success — by convention only",
            "Enforced by discipline, not by the compiler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Undefined Contract",
          "text": "When `err != nil`, other return values are undefined unless documented. `io.Reader` is the famous exception: it may return `n > 0` together with an error."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Constructing",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`errors.New(\"msg\")` returns `*errorString` — a pointer",
            "Two `errors.New` with the same text are never `==`",
            "`fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %v\", name, err)` flattens cause to text"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "String Style",
          "items": [
            "lowercase, no capitalisation",
            "no trailing punctuation",
            "they get concatenated into chains",
            "`openConfig: read /etc/app.conf: denied`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Errors as Data & the errors Package",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors Are Data",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stored in slices, sent over channels, compared",
            "Constructed at init time as package values",
            "The `errors` package is tiny: New, Is, As, Unwrap, Join",
            "Power lives in the interface, not in the package"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "ch := make(chan error, n)",
            "go func() { ch <- work(id) }()",
            "if err := <-ch; err != nil {",
            "  return err // just a value moving",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Whole Package",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Func",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`New`",
              "make a value"
            ],
            [
              "`Is`",
              "value anywhere in chain?"
            ],
            [
              "`As`",
              "type anywhere in chain?"
            ],
            [
              "`Unwrap`",
              "one step down"
            ],
            [
              "`Join`",
              "merge independent errors"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Built At Init",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var (",
            "  ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"not found\")",
            "  ErrClosed   = errors.New(\"closed\")",
            ")"
          ],
          "note": "one alloc each, at program start"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Because They Are Values",
          "text": "Map them to HTTP codes, fan them over channels, or list the expected error in a table-driven test. ==No other machinery needed.=="
        }
      ]
    },
