        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Custom Types",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "type PathError struct {",
            "  Op, Path string",
            "  Err error // the wrapped cause",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "func (e *PathError) Error() string {",
            "  return e.Op + \" \" + e.Path // + cause",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Implement `Error()` on `*T` if the type is large or compared",
            "Pointer types make identity comparison meaningful and cheap",
            "Fields carry status codes, offsets, retry hints",
            "Never return a zero-value custom struct as an error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "func NewParseError(l int, e error) error {",
            "  return &ParseError{Line: l, Err: e}",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Context Goes",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Add context at the boundary you cross, not at every frame",
            "One wrap per layer, never one per call",
            "No redundant naming: `getUser: getUser failed`",
            "Return `nil` explicitly on success"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "if err != nil {",
            "  return fmt.Errorf(\"load %q: %w\", p, err)",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Hot Loop Trap",
          "text": "`errors.New` inside a loop allocates every iteration. Hoist it to a package-level `var` and return the same value each time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Stdlib Error Shapes & Pointer Receivers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stdlib Shapes",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`*os.PathError` — op, path, syscall cause",
            "`*net.OpError` — network op, addr, cause",
            "`*json.SyntaxError` — byte `Offset`",
            "`*strconv.NumError` — func, input, cause"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var pe *os.PathError",
            "if errors.As(err, &pe) {",
            "  log.Print(pe.Op, pe.Path)",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "the fields are the whole point"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Value Or Pointer",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Receiver",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`func (e *T)`",
              "only `*T` is an error"
            ],
            [
              "`func (e T)`",
              "both `T` and `*T` work"
            ],
            [
              "large struct",
              "always take `*T`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pointer identity makes `==` and `errors.Is` cheap and exact",
            "A value receiver copies the struct on every call",
            "Returning `T` when callers match `*T` makes `As` fail silently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Before You Return",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Return `nil` explicitly — never a zero-value struct",
            "Lowercase text, no trailing full stop",
            "One wrap per layer you actually cross",
            "Hoist fixed-text errors to package vars"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Constructor, Not Literal",
          "text": "Export `NewParseError(...)` instead of the bare struct. You can add fields later without breaking every caller's composite literal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Sentinel Errors",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What A Sentinel Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"not found\")",
            "// exported signal, comparable identity"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Exported package-level value used purely as a signal",
            "Must be a `var` — no `const` of pointer type exists",
            "Once callers compare against it, it is public API",
            "You can never change or remove it after that"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Naming Rule",
          "items": [
            "`Err` prefix for values: `ErrClosed`",
            "`Error` suffix for types: `SyntaxError`",
            "Value signals vs data-carrying types"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Classics",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Sentinel",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`io.EOF`",
              "normal end of read"
            ],
            [
              "`io.ErrUnexpectedEOF`",
              "truncated stream"
            ],
            [
              "`sql.ErrNoRows`",
              "empty query result"
            ],
            [
              "`os.ErrNotExist`",
              "missing path"
            ],
            [
              "`context.Canceled`",
              "ctx cancelled"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`context.DeadlineExceeded` — the timeout signal",
            "`io.EOF` is not a failure, it is termination",
            "Treating `io.EOF` as an error is a bug, not strictness"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Compare, Never ==",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "if errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) {",
            "  return 404 // survives any wrapping",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Brittle Text Match",
          "text": "`strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"not found\")` breaks the moment anyone rewords the message. Never branch on error text."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Typed and Const Sentinels",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "type errString string",
            "func (e errString) Error() string {",
            "  return string(e)",
            "}",
            "const ErrX = errString(\"x\") // immutable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`type errNotFound struct{}` plus a singleton `var` gives both",
            "Identity matching and type matching from one declaration",
            "A caller can reassign your exported `var ErrX`",
            "The const trick removes that hazard entirely"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When To Export One",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Only when callers must branch on that exact condition",
            "Sentinels couple caller to package — simplest signal there is",
            "Carrying data? Use a custom type instead",
            "Behaviour check `interface{ Temporary() bool }` beats identity"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Wrapping With %w",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The %w Verb",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "return fmt.Errorf(\"query user %d: %w\",",
            "  id, err) // cause kept, not flattened"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Verb",
            "Chain",
            "Use for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`%w`",
              "preserved",
              "cause is contract"
            ],
            [
              "`%v`",
              "severed",
              "hide internals"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Text reads top-down, the cause chain is preserved bottom-up",
            "`%v` renders the cause as text and cuts the chain",
            "`%w` keeps it inspectable by `Is` and `As`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What You Get Back",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`%w` returns an unexported `*fmt.wrapError`",
            "Fields: `msg string` and `err error` — nothing more",
            "`errors.Unwrap(err)` calls `Unwrap` once",
            "Returns `nil` if the error does not implement it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "func (e *ParseError) Unwrap() error {",
            "  return e.Err // the whole contract",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Trees, Not Just Chains",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Multiple `%w` in one `fmt.Errorf` (Go 1.20+) gives `Unwrap() []error`",
            "That is a tree, not a chain",
            "Joined errors format one per line",
            "`Is`/`As` traverse every branch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "err := errors.Join(e1, e2, nil)",
            "// nils skipped; nil if all are nil",
            "// Unwrap() []error exposes both"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "handler",
              "service",
              "repo",
              "sql: no rows"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Wrapping Is An API Decision",
          "text": "Exposing the cause lets callers depend on it forever. Wrap deliberately; use `%v` when the internal type must stay private."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Join For Parallel Failures",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var errs []error",
            "for _, f := range fields {",
            "  errs = append(errs, check(f))",
            "}",
            "return errors.Join(errs...)"
          ],
          "note": "nil entries are dropped for you"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shape",
            "Unwrap method"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "single `%w`",
              "`Unwrap() error`"
            ],
            [
              "multi `%w`",
              "`Unwrap() []error`"
            ],
            [
              "`errors.Join`",
              "`Unwrap() []error`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Join` for **independent** failures: validation, fan-out workers",
            "`%w` chains for layered context — one wrap per layer",
            "`errgroup.Wait` keeps only the **first** error and cancels the rest"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Wrapping Traps: nil and Pre-1.13 Code",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Traps",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "nil And Legacy",
          "items": [
            "`%w` on nil renders `%!w(<nil>)`",
            "Guard `err != nil` before wrapping",
            "Pre-1.13: `pkg/errors` `Wrap`/`Cause`",
            "`%w` + `errors.Is` replaced it"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "errors.Is — Match By Identity",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Is Reports",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reports whether any error in the chain matches `target`",
            "Not just the outermost one — the whole chain",
            "Wrapping stays transparent to the caller"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "err == target",
              "err.Is(target)",
              "errors.Unwrap",
              "repeat until nil"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`==` used only when the target type is comparable",
            "Non-comparable targets are skipped, never panic",
            "`Unwrap() []error` is walked depth-first, any branch wins",
            "`errors.Is(err, nil)` is true only when `err` is nil — use `err == nil`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Custom Matching",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "func (e *MyErr) Is(t error) bool {",
            "  return t == ErrNotFound // declare alias",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`os.ErrNotExist` matches a `*os.PathError` this way",
            "The path error wraps a syscall errno, custom `Is` bridges them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Everyday Uses",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "if errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded) {",
            "  return retryLater() // correct timeout test",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The raw deadline value is almost always wrapped by then",
            "`io.Copy` reports EOF as **success** — it returns `nil`",
            "`bufio` hands back `io.EOF` bare, never wrapped",
            "`*url.Error` and decoders do wrap their reader's error",
            "Use `Is`: you cannot know which layer wrapped"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Price and Limits",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Is` is O(depth) pointer comparisons — trivial",
            "Safe inside handlers and middleware",
            "Avoid inside inner loops over millions of errors",
            "Do not use `Is` to test types — that job is `errors.As`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Test",
            "Finds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`==`",
              "exact value only"
            ],
            [
              "`errors.Is`",
              "value anywhere in chain"
            ],
            [
              "`errors.As`",
              "type anywhere in chain"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Silent Swallow",
          "text": "A custom `Is` that always returns `true` makes every match succeed, quietly absorbing unrelated errors. And `if err == sql.ErrNoRows` breaks the moment any layer wraps with `%w`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "errors.As — Match By Type",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shape Of The Call",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var pe *os.PathError",
            "if errors.As(err, &pe) {",
            "  log.Print(pe.Path) // structured field",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Finds the first error in the chain assignable to `*target`",
            "Assigns it, then returns `true`",
            "Target: non-nil pointer to an error type, or to an interface",
            "Never read the target after a `false` result"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Walk Order",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "assignable?",
              "err.As(target)",
              "Unwrap",
              "repeat"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same traversal `Is` uses, different test at each node",
            "Custom hook: `func (e *MyErr) As(target any) bool`",
            "It lets a type present itself as another type"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Behaviour Matching",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var ne net.Error",
            "if errors.As(err, &ne) && ne.Timeout() {",
            "  retry()",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An interface target gives behaviour-based matching",
            "`var t interface{ Timeout() bool }` works the same way",
            "Use `As` for errors carrying data, `Is` for pure signals"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var se *json.SyntaxError",
            "if errors.As(err, &se) {",
            "  log.Print(se.Offset) // parse position",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Panic Cases To Memorise",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "nil target",
            "non-pointer target",
            "pointer to a non-error, non-interface type"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Address, Not Value",
          "text": "`errors.As(err, pe)` compiles fine and panics at run time. It is always `&pe`."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two More Snags",
          "items": [
            "Matching `*MyErr` when code returned `MyErr` by value fails",
            "Different types, so `As` returns false",
            "`As` uses `reflectlite` for assignability",
            "A few hundred ns — fine outside hot loops"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Panic: Mechanics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What panic Does",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stops normal execution of the current goroutine",
            "Runs deferred functions up the stack, LIFO per frame",
            "Prints the stack trace and exits with status 2",
            "Panic value is `any` — usually an `error` or a string"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Runtime-generated ones carry a `runtime.Error`",
            "Unwinding is not free: no inlining, defer processing, stack walk",
            "Far more expensive than returning an error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Runtime Panics",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "nil map write",
            "nil pointer dereference",
            "index out of range",
            "slice bounds out of range"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "integer divide by zero",
            "failed type assertion",
            "send on a closed channel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scope and Tracing",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Panic is per-goroutine but fatal for the process",
            "One unrecovered panic in any goroutine kills everything",
            "`runtime.Goexit` runs defers but ends only that goroutine",
            "No panic value, no crash"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "GOTRACEBACK",
          "items": [
            "`none` — message only",
            "`single` — default, one goroutine",
            "`all` — every goroutine",
            "`system` / `crash` — runtime frames, core dump"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Panicking inside a deferred call during a panic prints both",
            "Labelled `panic: ... [recovered]` in the output"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When To Panic",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Programmer errors and impossible states only",
            "Never for bad input, missing files, or dead networks",
            "Stdlib panics rarely and loudly",
            "`strconv` never panics — it returns `*NumError`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Panics",
            "Why"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`regexp.MustCompile`",
              "init-time literal"
            ],
            [
              "`template.Must`",
              "init-time parse"
            ],
            [
              "`sync.WaitGroup`",
              "negative counter"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "func mustEnv(k string) string {",
            "  v, ok := os.LookupEnv(k)",
            "  if !ok { panic(\"missing env \" + k) }",
            "  return v",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Not A Panic At All",
          "text": "`fatal error:` — concurrent map writes, all-goroutines deadlock, out of memory — bypasses defers and cannot be recovered. `Must*` wrappers exist for package init, where failure is unrecoverable anyway."
        }
      ]
